WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.000
[Music]

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:31.066
[Narrator:] Middletown, a quiet American community,

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:41.499
after a busy day at the office, the shop, or perhaps one of the local plants.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.700
But some plants like this newspaper operate 24 hours a day.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.800
Yes, news is always in the making.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.033
[Music]

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:01.366
Mad dog bites 18 here.

00:01:01.366 --> 00:01:03.166
[Radio host:] Here's a special announcement.

00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:07.032
The county health department has declared an epidemic of rabies in Butler County.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:11.933
Eighty-nine cases of rabies in dogs have occurred in the county during the past three months,

00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:15.533
and 165 persons have received vaccine treatment.

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:19.966
Today 18 people were bitten by one rabid dog roaming through Middletown.

00:01:19.966 --> 00:01:23.499
This dog is...advise you to wash the wound with soap and warm running water,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.166
then consult your physician and the county health department

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:30.232
to determine whether vaccine treatment will be required.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:34.766
The county health department has called in Dr. Joseph Fisher, the state public health veterinarian,

00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:39.699
and Dr. Burton Richards, the rabies control expert from the United States Public Health Service,

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.833
to set up emergency control measures.

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:46.033
If you are the owner of a dog who's been bitten, take your pet to the nearest animal clinic

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.033
or humane shelter for vaccination.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:52.633
Authorities say that once rabies develops in man or animal, it is a hundred percent fatal.

00:01:52.633 --> 00:01:56.299
Get in touch with your physician or veterinarian as soon as possible.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.800
Be sure to keep your pets indoors until the county health department

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.400
declares that this epidemic is under control.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.766
For further news, stay tuned to this station.

00:02:04.766 --> 00:02:18.299
[Music]

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.933
[Narrator:] This dying animal, paralyzed and helpless, has caused fear, anxiety,

00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:26.199
and costly damage in Middletown.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:33.000
Picked up by the dog warden, the dog is taken to the local humane shelter for observation.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.833
The dog died and its head was sent to the health department.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:41.866
Here in a small, isolated room, the brain is removed from the skull

00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:45.466
for examination for positive evidence of rabies.

00:02:45.466 --> 00:02:49.732
It is safe to delay human vaccine treatment provided that laboratory facilities

00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:52.333
are immediately available.

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:57.233
Diagnosis is determined by the finding of Negri bodies within any portion of the brain-containing

00:02:57.233 --> 00:03:03.933
nerve cells, but Negri bodies are most prevalent in the Ammon's horn.

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:07.299
The dog had rabies.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:15.000
Dr. Brown was notified immediately and injections began, 14 painful injections, one every day.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.033
The strain took its toll on the parents as well as the child.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:25.033
Tommy would get well, 18 people in Middletown would get well,

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:31.466
but they would always remember that once rabies develops, it's 100 percent fatal.

00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:37.232
In the meantime, the emergency program to control the epidemic was in full swing.

00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:41.199
[Music]

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:47.166
[Loudspeaker mounted on car:] Protect human lives, prevent rabies.

00:03:47.166 --> 00:03:53.532
[Music]

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:59.133
[Loudspeaker mounted on car:] Protect human lives, prevent rabies.

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:23.699
[Music]

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.433
[Loudspeaker mounted on car:] Have your dog vaccinated today.

00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:35.133
[Music]

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:39.566
[Loudspeaker mounted on car:] Have your dog vaccinated against rabies today.

00:04:39.566 --> 00:05:00.232
[Music]

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:03.366
[Narrator:] Through the cooperation of the entire community,

00:05:03.366 --> 00:05:06.732
80 percent of all dogs were immunized in one week.

00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:13.833
The emergency control program showed excellent results.

00:05:13.833 --> 00:05:18.099
Although these were emergency animal clinics, they were set up with authorized procedures

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.800
for inoculating all dogs in any community, in any state.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:28.166
Standard vaccination certificates were issued by the county health department.

00:05:28.166 --> 00:05:33.232
Owners were advised to inoculate their dogs at least once a year.

00:05:33.233 --> 00:05:41.466
To keep their dogs on leashes or confined at home for 30 days until the vaccine was fully effective.

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:47.132
All dogs were inoculated with a vaccine approved by the U.S. Bureau of Animal Industry.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:57.066
[Music]

00:05:57.066 --> 00:05:59.966
With rabies under control, the people of Middletown were determined

00:05:59.966 --> 00:06:04.032
to keep it out of the community for good.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:09.033
The state public health veterinarian called a meeting of all private practicing veterinarians,

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:13.866
physicians, public health officers, and leading citizens to set up a permanent,

00:06:13.866 --> 00:06:18.066
long-range control program in every community in the state.

00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:21.232
[Veterinarian:] And for that reason we have asked Dr. Richards to explain how

00:06:21.233 --> 00:06:27.899
the United States Public Health Service was coping with this problem.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:34.333
[Applause]

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:40.533
[Dr. Richards:] We know how to control rabies. Other countries have done so.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.166
We can do the same.

00:06:43.166 --> 00:06:50.199
Our farm quarantine measures require the inoculation of all dogs entering the United States,

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:54.466
yet millions of our own dogs are unprotected.

00:06:54.466 --> 00:06:59.366
Stray dogs must be reported to the local health department

00:06:59.366 --> 00:07:02.566
and properly impounded in humane shelters.

00:07:02.566 --> 00:07:09.166
Rabies in wild animals is also an important problem in many parts of the country.

00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:15.199
Our U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service is helping the states carry out trapping programs

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.233
during epidemics of rabies.

00:07:18.233 --> 00:07:24.199
Every year millions of dollars are lost to dairy farmers and cattle breeders.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:29.966
Thousands of injections are given to people bitten by rabid dogs.

00:07:29.966 --> 00:07:37.232
Parents and children suffer in fear. This need not be.

00:07:37.233 --> 00:07:42.333
We must recognize the seriousness of rabies.

00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:47.566
We must assume a personal responsibility.

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:54.399
Have our own dogs inoculated, and then get the rest of the community to do the same.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:05.100
Then the states, and the state themselves must join the National Rabies Control Program.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:11.333
We can win the fight against rabies.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:16.980
[Music]

